<title>PARAGUAY: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP GROUP DRAW FOR FIRST ROUND.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP GROUP DRAW FOR FIRST ROUND.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Group draw for the first round of the 1997 South American Libertadores Cup made on Thursday:</p>
<p>Group 1 - Paraguay and Bolivia</p>
<p>Group 2 - Argentina and Ecuador</p>
<p>Group 3 - Chile and Venezuela</p>
<p>Group 4 - Brazil and Peru</p>
<p>Group 5 - Colombia and Uruguay</p>
<p>Note: Top three clubs in each group qualify for the second round. Holders River Plate of Argentina have a bye to the second round.</p>
<p>Participants announced so far:</p>
<p>Argentina - Velez Sarsfield and Racing Club</p>
<p>(note: Velez won both championships played in the 1995/6 season. Racing Club won a playoff between the two second-placed teams)</p>
<p>Brazil - Cruzeiro (winners of Copa Brasil) and Brazilian champions (to be decided)</p>
<p>Chile - Champions Colo Colo plus second team to be decided by playoff.</p>
<p>Colombia - Deportivo Cali and Millonarios (1995/6 champions and runners-up)</p>
<p>Ecuador - Nacional with second team to be decided</p>
<p>Peru - Sporting Cristal (1996 champions), second team to be decided by playoff.</p>
<p>Venezuela - Minerven and Mineros.</p>
<p>Bolivia, Paraguay and Uruguay still to be decided.</p>
</text>
